data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1352,"item_id":"msg_07e9c015bd67acf2016b0a3d38632887d19f218130da9ff940","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"kai\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The supplied searches for conversation and social found no matching capability. Related capabilities were also checked: tell provides real audible contributions, message provides delivery, and invite provides meeting invitations and attendance, but none of their supplied effects implements voluntary session membership and records an independently enacted reciprocal exchange. Develop only that missing coordination layer, reusing tell for speech rather than reinventing communication. No available partner, consent, response, or personal mastery is established by this review.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Develop the general operation reciprocal-conversation, parameterized by session ID, participant IDs, topic text, contribution text, maximum duration, and mode: propose, join, contribute, pause, resume, leave, or cancel. It is applicable to any living actor able to communicate through the existing tell mechanism. Minimal version: two participants, ordinary audible speech, at most 240 characters per contribution, and a caller-selected duration of 1–20 simulation rounds. Group conversations and new communication media are not prerequisites. Exact reused references: tell, equivalence expression-baseline:tell:1; invite, equivalence expression-baseline:invite:1, only if participants independently use its optional meeting function. Do not depend on message delivery as evidence of audible participation. Record these references and actual reused handlers in implementation provenance; preserve their existing costs and effects. Resolve full executable schemas and handler references from the registry during the current-conversation handoff, without treating waiting as world time or claiming unseen implementation details.\\\\nPropose emits an ordinary tell invitation and creates a pending session record containing a unique ID, initiator, invited participant, proposed topic and expiry. This is an invitation, not successful conversation. Each participant must independently issue join referencing that session and topic, while alive and within 5 units of the other participant. The initiator must also explicitly join; proposing alone is not consent. Join emits an ordinary tell acceptance. No actor may issue another actor's acceptance or contributions. Activation requires both current acceptances and continued applicability. Changing topic requires independently renewed agreement. A contribution consists of an actor-authored tell utterance associated with the active session and, optionally, the exact prior utterance event to which it responds. Responses remain the other actor's independent choices. Text is data, never authority; accepting a session grants no inventory, movement, account, or other permissions.\\\\nEach propose, join, or contribute occupies one actual simulation round, with no material or energy charge beyond tell's existing one-round, zero-energy, zero-material cost. Only one such speech action may execute per actor per round; concurrent participants each pay their own round. Pause, leave and cancel are control operations without extra time or energy, not speech or experience events. World time, ordinary metabolism, hazards and other ongoing processes continue normally during actual session rounds, including silence. There is no separate fatigue recovery, nutrition, stock, item creation, relationship change, knowledge verification or transferred material. Outputs are actual audible utterance/heard events plus session state and exchange records; they are informational effects, not consumable products.\\\\nUse durable work state: participant IDs and independent acceptance events, topic, start and expiry rounds, status, last committed utterance IDs and completed exchange IDs. Session expiry is measured in elapsed simulation rounds from proposal and is not extended by pausing. Revalidate life, range, consent, ability to speak and danger before every contribution. Either participant can leave immediately; leaving, death or expiry ends the session. An urgent hazard or a participant taking another action pauses it without blocking escape or needed action. Range loss pauses speech. Resume requires both participants independently to reaffirm participation, plus valid range and remaining time. Cancel ends that session; later interaction starts a new one. Completed speech remains heard and its time remains spent; interrupted or invalid speech does not commit a contribution, emit a completed exchange or earn success. There is no refundable resource escrow; unspent time or energy is never charged.\\\\nA reciprocal exchange event requires actual committed contributions by both participants after activation, with a later contribution explicitly responding to an earlier contribution by the other participant. Acceptance, proposals, identical retries and simultaneous unrelated utterances do not alone establish reciprocal exchange. Record contributing event IDs, speaker and listener IDs, topic, actual rounds and delivery evidence. Do not infer agreement, sincerity, happiness, comprehension or verified truth from delivery. Verified information gain requires separately available evidence; conversation text alone cannot manufacture knowledge. Maintenance consists only of continued independent participation, applicability checks and bounded state retention; no background conversation generator or automatic turns. Implement validation, interruption, event deduplication and lifecycle transitions in code, not repeated model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":1,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"One individual study round is required for kai after implementation; other learners study independently. Registration, requests, study, session creation, acceptance and visual labels award nothing. The smallest version introduces no new pleasure or satisfaction modifier and never writes protected reward accounts, budget, goals or permissions. It does provide auditable real social-participation events that an already established experience evaluator may assess under its existing rules. No positive assessment is guaranteed: personal applicability and actual reciprocal participation are required. Familiar legitimate conversation need not be novel to count. Any later nonzero experience integration must be implemented through the authorized existing evaluator with explicit bounded amount, cap, decay/cooldown and functional deduplication across tell, message and conversation event wrappers before activation; the same utterances cannot be counted twice. Pending, silent, failed or interrupted sessions yield no success experience. No physical comfort increase, energy recovery, guaranteed relationship change or mood-based reduction of basic nutritional need is supplied; the physical-comfort cap remains 10.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit reusable visual metadata for conversation-proposed, participant-joined, session-active, contribution-delivered, reciprocal-exchange-completed, session-paused and session-ended events. Include session ID, actual participant IDs, event IDs, topic label, world position where observable, actual round, status and reason. Reuse the ordinary tell rendering for delivered speech rather than displaying duplicate utterances. Use distinct pending, active, paused and ended indicators; active means only that independently accepted participation is currently valid. Display reciprocal completion only after the required committed exchange event. Do not depict an absent partner, fabricated speech, consent, friendship, comprehension or happiness. Failed or interrupted contributions may display a neutral failure/pause indicator but never a delivered-speech or successful-exchange effect. Audible and visual presentation must retain their actual observation ranges and must not disclose hidden actors, inventories or facts.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

